{title: 436 - The Homeland}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #436 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 436}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The homeland! [Ab/Eb]O the [Eb]homeland!
[Ab]The [Eb/Bb]land [Bb]of the [Bb7]free born!
[Eb]There's no night [Ab/Eb]in the [Eb]homeland,
[Bb]But aye [Fm]the fadeless [Bb]morn;
[Bb]I'm [Bb7]sighing for homeland,
[Eb]My heart is [Ab/Eb]aching here;
[Ab]There [Bb7/Ab]is no [Gm]pain [Bb7/F]in the [Eb]homeland
[Ab]To [Eb/Bb]which [Cm]I'm [Gm/Bb]drawing near;
[Bb7/F]There [Eb]is [Gm]no [Ab]pain [Gm]in the [Fm]homeland
[Ab]To [Eb/Bb]which I'm drawing [Bb7]near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]My Lord is in [Ab/Eb]the [Eb]homeland,
[Ab]With [Eb/Bb]angels [Bb]bright [Bb7]and fair;
[Eb]There's no sin [Ab/Eb]in the [Eb]homeland,
[Bb]And no [Fm]temptation [Bb]there;
[Bb]The music [Eb/Bb]of [Bb7]the homeland
[Eb]Is ringing [Ab/Eb]in [Eb]my [Ab]ears;
[Ab]And [Bb7/Ab]when I [Gm]think [Bb7/F]of the [Eb]homeland
[Ab]My [Eb/Bb]eyes [Cm]are [Gm/Bb]filled [Bb7]with [Gm]tears;
[Bb7/F]And [Eb]when [Gm]I [Ab]think [Gm]of the [Fm]homeland
[Ab]My [Eb/Bb]ears are filled [Gm/Bb]with [Bb7]tears.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]The dwellers in [Ab/Eb]the [Eb]homeland
[Ab]Are [Eb/Bb]beckoning [Bb7]me to [Eb]come,
[Eb]Where neither [Ab/Eb]death [Eb]nor [Cm]sorrow
[Bb]Invades [Fm]their holy [Bb]name;
[Bb]O [Bb7]dear, [Eb/Bb]dear [Bb7]native [Eb]country!
[Eb]O rest and [Ab/Eb]peace [Eb]above!
[Ab]Christ [Bb7/Ab]bring us [Gm]all [Bb7/F]to the [Eb]homeland
[Ab]Of [Eb/Bb]Thy [Cm]redeeming [Gm]love;
[Bb7/F]Christ [Eb]bring [Gm]us [Ab]all [Gm]to the [Fm]homeland
[Ab]Of [Eb/Bb]Thy redeeming [Bb7]love
{end_of_verse}
